IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-declarations`

-- Statutory Declarations Act 1959 (Cth) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or against the Statutory Declarations Regulations 2023, which are not deposited.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_statutory-declarations-act-1959_baseline.py).
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel): d034, 1 June 2026, Daniel (30) is an
-- authorised witness by virtue of his practising certificate. That he is enrolled on the roll of the Supreme Court of
-- Western Australia as a legal practitioner (which a practising certificate presupposes) is ASSUMED; from that, reg 6(a) of
-- the Statutory Declarations Regulations 2023 makes him a prescribed person, and the encoding now decides it. Daniel's clients and the other
-- people are the encoder's illustrations, not scenario events.

§ `Declarations`

`Daniel witnesses a client on paper, in person (d034)` MEANS `Declaration` WITH
    `in the approved form` IS TRUE
    `how I signed` IS `by hand on a physical form`
    `my signing method identifies me and shows my intention` IS TRUE
    `my signing method was reliable enough or proven in fact` IS TRUE
